# FINDINGS — register (slim HOT tier)

> Aggregates every finding from issues/reviews/audits into one closure-tracked list.
> Status: OPEN | CLOSED | ACCEPTED. `rt?` = needs live validation (not just inspection).
> Assign the next `F-NN` from the highest existing ID, including closed findings (never reuse);
> move resolved → CLOSED with evidence; never delete a row.
> **One line per finding here — Finding ≤ ~160 chars, Next step ≤ ~110.** Full narrative for every
> row lives in `{{DETAILS}}` (search the `F-NN`; the `Detail` column says `DETAIL` when there is
> more there). This file stays scannable.
> **Size budget: ≤ 36 KB.** Narrative goes to the detail file, not here.
> **Next free ID: F-1** (recompute from this file immediately before assigning — never from memory).
> **⚠ ID collision hazard:** this register has no allocator. Two sessions running the same day WILL
> pick the same `F-NN` unless each reads the register immediately before assigning (one writer).

